{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles","doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"feedbackArcSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The heuristic orders the vertices in a sequence and takes every edge that points leftward"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in it, and every self-loop. It repeatedly removes a sink (placed at the right end of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence), else a source (at the left end), else the vertex whose out-degree minus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-degree is largest (at the left end), with the least "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" offset on ties. Sinks and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sources are removed in the order they became one, starting from "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops do not count toward degrees; parallel edges count once each. On an acyclic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph the result is empty, and for every graph, removing (or reversing) the returned edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves no directed cycle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Eades, Lin and Smyth, “A fast and effective heuristic for the feedback arc set problem”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Information Processing Letters 47(6), 1993. The largest-difference vertices are kept in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary heap so that ties go to the least offset.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O((n + m) log n) time, O(n + m) memory.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/feedbackarcset()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges that Eades, Lin and Smyth’s greedy heuristic removes to make the graph acyclic,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", ascending: a feedback arc set, small in practice but not minimum."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Every self-loop is in it: arcs 0 → 0, 0 → 1, 1 → 0 give positions [0, 2]."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/feedbackArcSet()"},"metadata":{"title":"feedbackArcSet()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6CyclesE14feedbackArcSetSay5Edges_5IndexQZGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cycles"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"feedbackArcSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/feedbackArcSet()":{"title":"feedbackArcSet()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"feedbackArcSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/feedbackArcSet()","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/feedbackarcset()","abstract":[{"text":"The edges that Eades, Lin and Smyth’s greedy heuristic removes to make the graph acyclic,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":", ascending: a feedback arc set, small in practice but not minimum.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Every self-loop is in it: arcs 0 → 0, 0 → 1, 1 → 0 give positions [0, 2].","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"title":"DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Edges","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols","role":"collection"},"doc://Cycles/documentation/Cycles":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles","abstract":[],"title":"Cycles","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cycles","role":"collection"}}}